    "notes": [
      "Hot shop along the back wall: glory-hole drum is the warm focal light, lehr to its right, gaffer bench and marver in front with a clear swing aisle.",
      "Finished glass sits on limestone columns and a walnut case on a stone pad to the right. Cullet bins and wall shelves line the left with a 0.9 m reach aisle.",
      "Glass is opaque Toon colour with dark mouths and light lips. No alpha glass, so the furnace glow does not fight transparency sorting.",
      "Dining chairs face +Z at rotationY 0 (backrest toward -Z). Marver and cold-shop chairs are rotated pi so they face their work surfaces."
    ]
  },
